## Step 4: Bot Overview Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet for the bot overview analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# Placeholder Data (replace with real data retrieval)
bot_metrics = pd.DataFrame({
    "Bot Name": ["Bot A", "Bot B", "Bot C", "Bot D"],
    "Trades Executed": [120, 95, 140, 80],
    "Success Rate (%)": [65, 55, 75, 60],
    "Total Profit (£)": [5000, 3000, 7000, 2000]
}).set_index("Bot Name")

historical_data = {
    "Bot A": np.cumsum(np.random.randint(-50, 100, size=50)),
    "Bot B": np.cumsum(np.random.randint(-30, 80, size=50)),
    "Bot C": np.cumsum(np.random.randint(-70, 120, size=50)),
    "Bot D": np.cumsum(np.random.randint(-20, 60, size=50)),
}

# Page Title
st.title("🤖 Bot Overview")

# Bot Metrics
st.subheader("Bot Metrics")
st.dataframe(bot_metrics, use_container_width=True)

# Historical Performance Trends
st.subheader("Historical Performance Trends")
bot_selection = st.selectbox("Select Bot", list(historical_data.keys()))
bot_history_df = pd.DataFrame({"Trade #": range(1, 51), "Cumulative Profit": historical_data[bot_selection]}).set_index("Trade #")
st.line_chart(bot_history_df)

# Bot Rankings
st.subheader("Bot Rankings")
sorted_bot_metrics = bot_metrics.sort_values(by="Total Profit (£)", ascending=False)
st.dataframe(sorted_bot_metrics, use_container_width=True)
```

